/*--- Choupo stream state.  Every DIMENSIONAL value carries its unit; the parser converts to SI.
     componentMolarFlows is the OVERALL material (all phases); a phases{} block, when present,
     is a decomposition that sums back to it exactly. ---*/

/*  DESIGN BASIS (2026-10-06).  BD is adiabatic: this air both pays the latent
    heat and carries the water away, so it is sized for the RICHEST point of the
    sweep (RawJuice sucrose 0.160), where the powder must lose 245.7 kg/h to reach
    its isotherm's X_eq.  At 150 kmol/h (this file's earlier value) the exhaust
    saturated at ~148 kg/h on four of the six points and the powder left wetter
    than X_eq ([saturation-bound]; DEV.md 4c C37 item 3 is the rule that says so).
    At 300 kmol/h every point reaches the isotherm, the worst exhaust leaving at
    a_w = 0.87 -- a margin, not a coincidence of the last digit.  Same humidity as
    before (6.5 mol% water), same 380 K.  */

componentMolarFlows
{
    water    19.5 kmol/h;
    N2    280.5 kmol/h;
}

T               380 K;
P               100000 Pa;
phase           gas;
